  DIRECTION: a *proven* decay bound  ||T^n P|| <= C e^{-a lam n} (all n)  implies
             e^{-a Delta n} <= C e^{-a lam n}  =>  Delta >= lam - log C/(a n)  =>  Delta >= lam.
  => the direction is CORRECT (a norm UPPER bound gives a gap LOWER bound).
  ==> D1 (direction reversed) does NOT fire for this candidate.  This is the first
      candidate since C3 (trace/Alon-Boppana) to pass the direction account.
  But the hypothesis 'C e^{-a lam n} uniformly' is, by the displayed identity, equivalent
  to  Delta >= lam  in the limit: proving it IS proving the gap  (D2).

