W5  Lyapunov existence  !=  uniform hyperbolicity (exponential dichotomy)
    scalar cocycle Phi(n,0) = prod_{k<=n} e^{-Delta}(1+1/k) = e^{-Delta n}(n+1)
==============================================================================
     n       rate_n   C_n=||Phi||e^{Delta n}
     1   0.00685282                      2.0
    10   0.46021047                     11.0
   100   0.65384879                    101.0
  1000   0.69309125                   1001.0
 10000   0.69907896                  10001.0
100000   0.69988487                 100001.0
  -> the exponent exists and equals -0.7 (rate 0.7: rate_n -> 0.7 as log(n+1)/n -> 0),
     but C_n = n+1 -> inf: there is NO uniform C.  Lyapunov exponents are limits,
     not uniform bounds.
     A (L,a)-uniform lower bound needs the dichotomy CONDITION (uniform hyperbolicity),
     which is strictly stronger -- and in the beta coordinate it is literally
     'dist(spec_dichotomy, 0) >= a*lam', i.e. the gap restated in another coordinate.

