  mean >= min always, so a proven lower bound on the mean says NOTHING about the minimum,
  and the point value at beta=2.5 is not an ergodic average of anything.

==============================================================================
SUMMARY (candidate 3 / non-autonomous, Floquet, Lyapunov)
==============================================================================
 - DIRECTION: PASS.  A norm upper bound  ||T^n P|| <= C e^{-a lam n}  gives Delta >= lam.
   D1 does not fire.  (Second candidate ever to pass the direction account, after C3.)
 - unprojected the exponent is identically 0 (vacuum), i.e. vacuous (W1).
 - projected, the rate IS the gap (W2): the required uniform decay bound is equivalent
   to the conclusion -- the D2 horn.
 - beta-as-time: the exponent is the beta-infinity value, which asymptotic freedom sends
   to 0; the average decays like 1/B (W3) -- wrong half of the axis (D3).
 - certifying the point value a*m(2.5) by an average forces the window to collapse onto
   beta=2.5 (W4): the average is a different functional (D14).
 - uniform hyperbolicity is strictly stronger than Lyapunov existence (W5) and is the
   gap in the beta coordinate; ergodic means never control minima (W6).
 - D12 (no scale separation) never becomes the main cause: it is not even reached,
   because D3/D14/D2 fire first.  Prediction correction: D13 (carrier identically zero)
   does NOT fire either -- the carriers here are non-degenerate.
